\notedur sets how long notes sound, as a percentage of
their written duration. It applies to all instruments,
also to those created after it is called.
It does nothing by itself, it must be called with one of
its methods and a percentage (an integer from 1 to 100):

\notedur.normal 100

The methods are:

normal: notes without articulation
staccato: notes with a staccato (default 50)
staccatissimo: notes with a staccatissimo (default 25)
tenuto: notes with a tenuto (default 90)

For example, the line below makes staccato notes last
30% of their duration:

\notedur.staccato 30

Instruments created after this command is called, e.g.
with \insts.add, get the values it sets too.
Using a method name not listed above gives an
"unknown \notedur method" error.
